        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a short <strong>psychological visual novel</strong> that immerses the player in an <strong>unknown, surreal reality</strong> filled with blinding light, fragmented memories, and a mysterious presence known as <strong>Katrina</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You will follow the story of a nameless protagonists who finds themselves trapped in this strange dimension, where reality seems unstable and encounters with &quot;Her&quot; repeat over and over again. Each return may reveal something new - a fragment of truth, a different perspective, or another unanswered question.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game is focused on <strong>narrative, atmosphere, and emotion</strong> rather than traditional gameplay mechanics. It explores themes of <strong>loss, trauma, repetition, and human fragility</strong>, offering an unsettling but deeply personal experience.<br><br><strong>FEATURES</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Narrative-driven experience</strong>: uncover the mystery of Katrina and the world she controls through branching dialogues.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Atmospheric storytelling</strong>: explore endless blinding rooms and the strange rules of this reality.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Psychological depth</strong>: themes of grief, trauma, and fragile perception.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Multiple playthroughs</strong>: re-entering this reality may reveal new fragments and hidden meaning.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Audiovisual immersion</strong>: original soundtrack and sound design with sudden loud effects that heighten tension.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Length</strong>: approximately 1–2 hours of gameplay, depending on choices.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>CREATOR &amp; PUBLISHER</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This visual novel is created by an artist from the independent label <strong>AREYOULUVME¿</strong>, a creative collective known for supporting underground musicians, visual storytellers, and experimental creators worldwide.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The author is active across many projects in music, art, and interactive media, blending sound and narrative into unique cross-disciplinary works. This release is part of that larger creative journey, where music and story meet digital art.<br><br><strong>CONTENT WARNING</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This visual novel contains <strong>loud sounds, frightening imagery, and triggering themes</strong> (including trauma and loss).<br>It is <strong>not recommended</strong> for players sensitive to such content.<br><br><strong>ABOUT THE PUBLISHER</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >AREYOULUVME¿ is an independent label and creative collective that supports underground musicians, visual artists, and experimental storytellers across the globe. We publish music, interactive media, and cross-disciplinary projects, uniting artists under one vision: <strong>to create without boundaries</strong>.</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a short <strong>psychological visual novel</strong> that immerses the player in an <strong>unknown, surreal reality</strong> filled with blinding light, fragmented memories, and a mysterious presence known as <strong>Katrina</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You will follow the story of a nameless protagonists who finds themselves trapped in this strange dimension, where reality seems unstable and encounters with &quot;Her&quot; repeat over and over again. Each return may reveal something new - a fragment of truth, a different perspective, or another unanswered question.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game is focused on <strong>narrative, atmosphere, and emotion</strong> rather than traditional gameplay mechanics. It explores themes of <strong>loss, trauma, repetition, and human fragility</strong>, offering an unsettling but deeply personal experience.<br><br><strong>FEATURES</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Narrative-driven experience</strong>: uncover the mystery of Katrina and the world she controls through branching dialogues.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Atmospheric storytelling</strong>: explore endless blinding rooms and the strange rules of this reality.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Psychological depth</strong>: themes of grief, trauma, and fragile perception.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Multiple playthroughs</strong>: re-entering this reality may reveal new fragments and hidden meaning.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Audiovisual immersion</strong>: original soundtrack and sound design with sudden loud effects that heighten tension.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Length</strong>: approximately 1–2 hours of gameplay, depending on choices.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>CREATOR &amp; PUBLISHER</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This visual novel is created by an artist from the independent label <strong>AREYOULUVME¿</strong>, a creative collective known for supporting underground musicians, visual storytellers, and experimental creators worldwide.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The author is active across many projects in music, art, and interactive media, blending sound and narrative into unique cross-disciplinary works. This release is part of that larger creative journey, where music and story meet digital art.<br><br><strong>CONTENT WARNING</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This visual novel contains <strong>loud sounds, frightening imagery, and triggering themes</strong> (including trauma and loss).<br>It is <strong>not recommended</strong> for players sensitive to such content.<br><br><strong>ABOUT THE PUBLISHER</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >AREYOULUVME¿ is an independent label and creative collective that supports underground musicians, visual artists, and experimental storytellers across the globe. We publish music, interactive media, and cross-disciplinary projects, uniting artists under one vision: <strong>to create without boundaries</strong>.</p>",
        "short_description": "A short psychological visual novel about a surreal reality, endless blinding rooms, and the mysterious Katrina. Discover fragments of truth and face unsettling themes of trauma and memory.",
